  "factor_name": "Breadth-Switch Trend/Reversal",
  "version": "1.0",
  "calculation": {
    "expression": "clip((breadth20-0.50)/0.25,-1,1): blend ((return20/ann_vol30)*(g+1)/2) + ((-return5/ann_vol30)*(1-g)/2), then cross-sectional demean",
    "description": "A causal regime-conditioned cross-asset signal. When the fraction of assets with positive 20-day returns is broad, it favors risk-adjusted medium momentum; when breadth is narrow, it shifts toward short-term reversal. The signal is cross-sectionally demeaned and uses only completed historical prices."
  },
